@kujtimiihoxha Yeah, that aspect is a WIP. I made it adapt to the code width because it's trying to detect the required width for now, but in real world scenarios the user should usually set a fixed width.

It'll probably look better if each side takes 50% of the total width, and I plan to work on it.

Code wrapping and scrolling is planned as well (likely both supported as an option).

@raphamorim let's hold of on this for a little bit, this could lead to smaller models being confused and not behave as expected.

The truth is that 4o and sonnet 4 already support parallel tool calling the issue is that I did not implement it so that the tools get called in parallel reason for this is that I need to update the permissions module.

For now I'd say we hold this. I will review the permissions stuff when I am done with the TUI updates.

@meowgorithm

1. <kbd>shift+hjkl</kbd> are already bind, just not shown on the help menu. Do you want to also show them on the help menu or is showing <kbd>shift+arrows</kbd> there enough?
2. Yeah, for this use case I think it makes sense to prevent scrolling beyond. I plan to add an option to diffview to control this. It should be pretty straighforward.

