Hi @ryx2 you can specify the API key in your global env also, and in the config files

Local project config
```
crush.json
// or
.crush.json
```

Global config (linux/mac)
```
$HOME/.config/crush/crush.json
```
Global config (win)
```
%LOCALAPPDATA%/crush/crush.json
```

You can configure any providers api key by setting it in the providers map

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://charm.land/crush.json",
  "providers": {
    "anthropic": {
      "api_key": "sk-....."
    }
  }
}
```
by env variable
```json
{
  "$schema": "https://charm.land/crush.json",
  "providers": {
    "anthropic": {
      "api_key": "$MY_ENV"
    }
  }
}
```
or even by running a script
```json
{
  "$schema": "https://charm.land/crush.json",
  "providers": {
    "anthropic": {
      "api_key": "$(bash myscript.sh)"
    }
  }
}
```

you can add a system prompt like this:

```json
{
  "options": {
    "context_paths": [
      "/home/user/.config/AGENT.md"
    ]
  }
}
```

drop it in `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/crush/crush.json`

