@richardARPANET if you are using deepseek through openrouter, you need to set the openrouter key, not the deepseek key.

if you're using it through deepseek's platform, you'll need to add the provider configuration to your `crush.json`, something like:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://charm.land/crush.json",
  "providers": {
    "deepseek": {
      "name": "DeepSeek",
      "base_url": "Deepseek's OPEN AI compatible URL",
      "api_key": "$DEEPSEEK_API_KEY",
      "type": "openai",
      "models": [
        {
          "name": "Model name",
          "id": "model_name",
          "context_window": 1234,
          "default_max_tokens": 1234
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

If you haven't done that, the options that'll be available are not from deepseek itself, they are from Lambda and Openrouter:

